Description
Create comprehensive telemetry instrumentation and Splunk dashboards to monitor and report on third-party container images throughout their lifecycle - from whitelisting through ingestion, approval, and security vulnerability detection.
 

Business Value
Enhanced visibility into third-party image usage and security posture
Proactive tracking of vulnerable images at ingestion
Data-driven decision making for image approval processes
Compliance and audit trail for image whitelisting
 

Acceptance Criteria
1. Telemetry Implementation
Instrument the following events with structured logging to Splunk:
 
Image Whitelisting Events:

Image whitelist request initiated
Image whitelist approved/rejected
Whitelist expiration/renewal
 
Image Ingestion Events:

New image ingestion attempt
Image validation status (pass/fail)
Vulnerability scan initiated
Vulnerability scan completed with severity levels (Critical/High/Medium/Low)
 
Image Approval Events:

Image approval workflow triggered
Image approved/rejected with reason
New release detected for existing whitelisted image
 

2. Metrics to Capture
Total images whitelisted (cumulative and time-based)
Images whitelisted per week/month
New images approved (time-series)
New releases detected (version tracking)
Vulnerabilities at ingestion:
Total vulnerable images
Breakdown by severity (Critical/High/Medium/Low)
Failure rate percentage
Ingestion failures:
Count and percentage
Failure reasons categorized
Time-to-approval metrics (average, P50, P95, P99)
Image source distribution (registry/vendor breakdown)
 

3. Splunk Dashboard Requirements
Dashboard 1: Image Whitelisting Overview

Total images whitelisted (current count)
Weekly/monthly whitelisting trend chart
Top image sources/vendors
Approval rate (approved vs rejected)
 
Dashboard 2: Security & Vulnerability Metrics

Vulnerable images at ingestion (pie chart by severity)
Vulnerability trend over time (line chart)
Failed ingestion count and reasons
Images requiring remediation (actionable list)
 
Dashboard 3: Operational Metrics

New releases tracked
Time-to-approval distribution
Processing pipeline health (success vs failure rates)
Alert panel for critical vulnerabilities detected
 
Dashboard 4: Compliance & Audit

Historical whitelist changes
Image lifecycle timeline
Policy violation tracking
 

4. Technical Implementation
Logging Standards:

Use structured JSON logging format
Include standard fields: timestamp, event_type, image_name, image_version, image_registry, status, vulnerability_count, severity_levels, user_id, action
Implement correlation IDs for tracking image lifecycle
 
Splunk Integration:

Configure Splunk HEC (HTTP Event Collector) endpoint
Implement retry logic and buffering
Set up index and sourcetype: index=security sourcetype=third_party_images
 
5. Alerts Configuration * Alert when critical vulnerabilities detected at ingestion

Alert on abnormal failure rates (>10%)
Weekly summary report generation
